6502 CPU Emulator
==================

A minimal emulator for the MOS 6502 microprocessor,
written in C++..

https://www.masswerk.at/6502/6502_instruction_set.html

STATUS
------
Implements the full official 6502 instruction set (151 opcodes(OP)):

  - Loads/stores: LDA, LDX, LDY, STA, STX, STY
  - Transfers: TAX, TAY, TXA, TYA, TSX, TXS
  - Stack: PHA, PHP, PLA, PLP
  - Logic: AND, EOR, ORA, BIT
  - Arithmetic: ADC, SBC, CMP, CPX, CPY
  - Inc/dec: INC, INX, INY, DEC, DEX, DEY
  - Shifts/rotates: ASL, LSR, ROL, ROR (accumulator and memory)
  - Control flow: JMP (absolute and indirect, including the real
    6502's indirect-JMP page-wrap hardware bug), JSR, RTS, all 8
    branches, BRK, RTI
  - Flags: CLC, CLD, CLI, CLV, SEC, SED, SEI, NOP
  - Stack pointer correctly increments/decrements on push/pop
  - Cycle counts implemented and tested for every instruction above,
    including page-cross penalties on absolute,X/Y and (indirect),Y

Limitations:
  - No BCD (decimal mode) arithmetic. The D flag is tracked but
    ADC/SBC always do binary math.
  - No undocumented opcodes (e.g. LAX, SAX).

BUILD
  make
  (equivalent by hand: g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra main.cpp -o emu)

RUN
  make run
  ./emu
